Python 3.12. Deskryptor Lazy ma tu także metodę __set__. Co wypisze program?
```python
class Lazy:
    def __init__(self, func):
        self.func = func
    def __set_name__(self, owner, name):
        self.name = name
    def __get__(self, obj, owner=None):
        if obj is None:
            return self
        print("compute")
        value = self.func(obj)
        obj.__dict__[self.name] = value
        return value
    def __set__(self, obj, value):
        obj.__dict__[self.name] = value

